    "detail": "privateMatches now decodes repeatedly: percent-encoding plus a new `\\\\+u` Unicode-escape pass, for up to 5 rounds. If the text is still changing after that, it returns a synthetic entry 0, so checkPrivateText, checkPrivateRange and blob scans block publication even when private-strings.txt is empty. Before this change, an empty denylist never blocked. These functions gate every commit, patch and blob the factory publishes, and the request (MCP tools plus a digest) didn't ask to change them. The extra layers also add up to 6\u00d7 the text to NFKC-normalize on large diffs."
